#provision("600.01", 3, level-label: "Section", title: [Introduction])[
  This handbook describes how the Exampleland FIR (ZXEX) runs its virtual air traffic control service.
] <p600-01>

#provision("600.01(1)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(1)", title: [Purpose])[
  This handbook is the single policy document for the Exampleland FIR. It replaces earlier informal notes and gives members one place to look for the rules that apply to them.
] <p600-01-1>

#provision("600.01(1)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  It is written for members, students, mentors, staff and visitors alike.
] <p600-01-1-a>

#provision("600.01(1)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  It sets policy. How-to guidance for individual positions lives in separate practice documents that carry no policy statements.
] <p600-01-1-b>

#provision("600.01(2)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(2)", title: [Applicability])[
  This handbook applies to every member of the FIR, whenever they are connected to the network or active in a related community space.
] <p600-01-2>

#provision("600.01(2)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Members are expected to read the handbook before their first session and to re-read it when a new version is announced.
] <p600-01-2-a>

#provision("600.01(2)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Where this handbook and a parent organization's policy disagree, the parent organization's policy applies.
] <p600-01-2-b>

#provision("600.01(3)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(3)", title: [Amendments])[
  Changes are shown in the published change summary and in the following manner:

  #list([Additions are shown #highlight[like this]\.], [Deletions are shown #strike[like this]\.], [Terms with a special meaning are shown #underline[like this] the first time they are used; see example-glossary \[600.01(1)\] for the definitions.])
] <p600-01-3>

#provision("600.01(4)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(4)", title: [Document family])[
  The handbook belongs to a small family of documents. Each has a clear purpose and a single owner.
] <p600-01-4>

#provision("600.01(4)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The handbook (this document) holds policy.
] <p600-01-4-a>

#provision("600.01(4)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Practice guides explain techniques for towers, terminals and the enroute sector.
] <p600-01-4-b>

#provision("600.01(4)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Short notices, valid for a limited period, carry temporary instructions; once a notice becomes permanent it is merged into the handbook.
] <p600-01-4-c>

#provision("600.01(5)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(5)", title: [Interpretation])[
  The words in this handbook have their everyday meaning unless a definition says otherwise.
] <p600-01-5>

#provision("600.01(5)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  "Shall" and "must" describe obligations. "Should" describes a recommendation that members follow unless they have a good reason not to.
] <p600-01-5-a>

#provision("600.01(5)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  "May" describes a permission and "may not" describes a prohibition.
] <p600-01-5-b>

#provision("600.01(5)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Headings are for convenience and do not change the meaning of the text under them.
] <p600-01-5-c>

#provision("600.01(6)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(6)", title: [Conduct])[
  Members behave in a way that makes the FIR a welcoming place, on the network and elsewhere.
] <p600-01-6>

#provision("600.01(6)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Members treat each other and pilots with courtesy, patience and respect.
] <p600-01-6-a>

#provision("600.01(6)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Controllers are fully engaged while logged on. Distractions such as games or unrelated browsing are not appropriate when traffic needs attention.
] <p600-01-6-b>

#provision("600.01(6)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Controller information lines are for information that helps pilots, for example:

  #list([the airports covered by the position;], [the expected log-off time;], [a link to the sector map;], [the availability of datalink services.])
] <p600-01-6-c>

#provision("600.01(6)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A member who breaks a rule may face counseling, a referral to the parent organization or removal from the FIR, at the discretion of the FIR Lead.
] <p600-01-6-d>

#provision("600.01(7)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(7)", title: [Version history])[
  The table lists the published versions of this handbook.

  #table(columns: 3, align: (left, left, left),
    table.header([Version], [Effective], [Summary]),
