  )
] <p600-01-7>

#provision("601", 2, level-label: "Subpart", title: [Training and Qualification], page-break: true)[

] <p601>

#provision("601.01", 3, level-label: "Section", title: [Training], page-break: true)[
  Training in the FIR is voluntary, unpaid and guided by the people who do it for the enjoyment of the community.
] <p601-01>

#provision("601.01(1)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(1)", title: [Principles])[
  Training aims to produce controllers who are safe, courteous and consistent.
] <p601-01-1>

#provision("601.01(1)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Students progress at their own pace. Nobody is ranked against anybody else.
] <p601-01-1-a>

#provision("601.01(1)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Feedback about a student is given to the student's mentor or instructor, not to the student directly and not in public.
] <p601-01-1-b>

#provision("601.01(1)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Mentors and instructors lead by example and are expected to know the documents listed in #link(<p600-01-4>)[\[600.01(4)\]]\.
] <p601-01-1-c>

#provision("601.01(2)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(2)", title: [Stages and expectations], whole: true)[
  The training path has four stages. The table summarises what each stage involves and how long it normally takes.#footnote[Durations are guidance only. A mentor may recommend a faster or slower pace for an individual student.]<fn-pace>

  #table(columns: 3, align: (left, left, left),
    table.header([Stage], [Focus], [Typical duration]),
    [Foundation], [Theory, tools and phraseology], [4 weeks],
    [Ground], [Ground and tower positions], [8 weeks],
    [Terminal], [Approach and departure], [12 weeks#footnote[The terminal stage includes at least two supervised sessions during an organized event.]<fn-cell>],
    [Enroute], [Centre sector], [12 weeks],
    table.cell(colspan: 2)[Summary of stages], [36 weeks],
  )
] <p601-01-2>

#provision("601.01(2)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A student prepares for every session by reading the assigned material beforehand.
] <p601-01-2-a>

#provision("601.01(2)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A student who cannot attend a booked session tells the mentor as early as possible.
] <p601-01-2-b>

#provision("601.01(2)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Students do not pressure staff for extra sessions or earlier assessments.
] <p601-01-2-c>

#provision("601.01(3)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(3)", title: [Assessment])[
  Each stage ends with a practical assessment. The assessment is run by an instructor who did not teach the student at that stage.
] <p601-01-3>

#provision("601.01(3)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The assessment covers phraseology, coordination and situational awareness.
] <p601-01-3-a>

#provision("601.01(3)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A student who does not pass receives written feedback and may retry after a cooling-off period of two weeks.
] <p601-01-3-b>

#provision("601.01(3)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Assessment results are recorded as described in #link(<p700-01-1>)[\[700.01(1)\]]\.
] <p601-01-3-c>

#provision("601.01(4)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(4)", title: [Mentors], keep: true)[
  Mentors give students extra practice between formal sessions. They are not instructors and do not run assessments.
] <p601-01-4>

#provision("601.01(4)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A mentor does not give a student their first lesson on a position.
] <p601-01-4-a>

#provision("601.01(4)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A mentor does not guide students at the mentor's own level.
] <p601-01-4-b>

#provision("601.01(4)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A mentor who wishes to run simulator sessions asks the Training Lead for approval first.
] <p601-01-4-c>

#provision("601.01(5)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(5)", title: [Resources])[
  Students have access to a small library of material.
] <p601-01-5>

#provision("601.01(5)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The library contains the handbook, the practice guides, recorded examples and a set of practice scenarios.
] <p601-01-5-a>

#provision("601.01(5)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Students tell their mentor about material that is out of date or unclear.
] <p601-01-5-b>

#provision("601.01(5)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Practice scenarios run on the simulator server and are booked in advance.
] <p601-01-5-c>

#provision("601.01(6)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(6)", title: [Special positions])[
  Some positions need an endorsement in addition to a stage.
] <p601-01-6>

#provision("601.01(6)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Endorsements are granted by the Training Lead after a practical assessment.
] <p601-01-6-a>

#provision("601.01(6)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  An endorsement lapses if the controller has not used it for twelve months.
] <p601-01-6-b>

#provision("601.01(6)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A controller whose endorsement has lapsed may regain it through a short refresher session.
] <p601-01-6-c>

#provision("601.01(7)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(7)", title: [Visitors])[
  Visitors from other regions are welcome.
] <p601-01-7>

#provision("601.01(7)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Visitors are expected to know the content of this handbook.
] <p601-01-7-a>

#provision("601.01(7)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Visitors who control fewer than three hours in a quarter may be removed from the visitor roster.
] <p601-01-7-b>

#provision("601.01(8)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(8)", title: [Instructors])[
  Instructors run assessments and guide students through the stages.
] <p601-01-8>

#provision("601.01(8)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  An instructor has controlled at least fifty hours in the FIR at the relevant level.
] <p601-01-8-a>

#provision("601.01(8)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  An instructor keeps written notes of every session and stores them in the central repository.
] <p601-01-8-b>

#provision("601.01(8)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  An instructor who stops teaching returns to the instructor's previous role without penalty.
] <p601-01-8-c>

#provision("601.01(8)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Instructors are recommended by the Training Lead and approved by the FIR Lead.
] <p601-01-8-d>

#provision("601.01(8)(e)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(e)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  An instructor never assesses a student whom the instructor mentored at that stage.
] <p601-01-8-e>

#provision("601.20", 3, level-label: "Section", title: [Duties of the Training Lead])[
  The Training Lead's duties are set out below in as much detail as the FIR needs.
] <p601-20>

#provision("601.20(1)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(1)", title: [Training program])[

] <p601-20-1>

#provision("601.20(1)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Run the training program.
] <p601-20-1-a>

#provision("601.20(1)(a)(i)", 6, level-label: "Subparagraph", label: "(i)", indent: 2)[
  Keep the list of students and mentors up to date.
] <p601-20-1-a-i>

#provision("601.20(1)(a)(i)(A)", 7, level-label: "Clause", label: "(A)", indent: 3)[
  Review the student list every month.
] <p601-20-1-a-i-A>

#provision("601.20(1)(a)(i)(A)(I)", 8, level-label: "Subclause", label: "(I)", indent: 4)[
  Remove students who have left the FIR.
] <p601-20-1-a-i-A-I>

#provision("601.20(1)(a)(i)(A)(II)", 8, level-label: "Subclause", label: "(II)", indent: 4)[
  Tell the Operations Lead when a student is removed.
] <p601-20-1-a-i-A-II>

#provision("601.20(1)(a)(i)(B)", 7, level-label: "Clause", label: "(B)", indent: 3)[
  Publish the updated list to staff within a week of each review.
] <p601-20-1-a-i-B>

#provision("601.20(1)(a)(ii)", 6, level-label: "Subparagraph", label: "(ii)", indent: 2)[
  Assign a mentor to every new student.
] <p601-20-1-a-ii>

#provision("601.20(1)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1, repealed: true)[
  Withdrawn on 2025-03-01.
] <p601-20-1-b>

#provision("601.20(1)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Report training progress to the FIR Lead every quarter.
] <p601-20-1-c>

#provision("601.20(2)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(2)", title: [Endorsements])[
  The Training Lead keeps the register of endorsements.
] <p601-20-2>

#provision("601.20(2)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The register shows the holder, the position and the date of the assessment.
] <p601-20-2-a>

#provision("601.20(2)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The register is reviewed together with the roster every quarter.
] <p601-20-2-b>

#provision("602", 2, level-label: "Subpart", title: [Operations], page-break: true)[

] <p602>

#provision("602.01", 3, level-label: "Section", title: [Controlling])[
  This section holds the rules for providing control service in the FIR. Controlling is a shared responsibility and every controller is expected to know it well.
] <p602-01>

#provision("602.01(1)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(1)", title: [Authorization])[
  A controller connects to a position only when authorized for it.
] <p602-01-1>

#provision("602.01(1)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Authorization is granted by the Operations Lead or a delegate and recorded in the roster.
] <p602-01-1-a>

#provision("602.01(1)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A student with a solo permission uses it only on the position named in the permission. Other positions are staffed only under the supervision of a mentor or instructor.
] <p602-01-1-b>

#provision("602.01(1)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The enroute positions require the enroute endorsement. All other positions are unrestricted.
] <p602-01-1-c>

#provision("602.01(2)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(2)", title: [Currency])[
  Controllers stay current by controlling regularly.
] <p602-01-2>

#provision("602.01(2)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Every controller controls at least three hours in each calendar quarter.
] <p602-01-2-a>

#provision("602.01(2)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A controller who expects to miss a quarter may request a leave of absence from the Operations Lead.
] <p602-01-2-b>

#provision("602.01(2)(b)(i)", 6, level-label: "Subparagraph", label: "(i)", indent: 2)[
  Only one leave is granted in any eighteen months.
] <p602-01-2-b-i>

#provision("602.01(2)(b)(ii)", 6, level-label: "Subparagraph", label: "(ii)", indent: 2)[
  A leave lasts no longer than six months.
] <p602-01-2-b-ii>

#provision("602.01(2)(b)(iii)", 6, level-label: "Subparagraph", label: "(iii)", indent: 2)[
  A leave ends as soon as the controller connects to control.
] <p602-01-2-b-iii>

#provision("602.01(2)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A controller who misses two consecutive quarters without a leave may be marked inactive and may be asked to recertify before returning to a position.
] <p602-01-2-c>

#provision("602.01(3)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(3)", title: [Releases and handoffs], keep: true)[
  #block(sticky: true)[Departures from ZXAA are released by the approach position and handed off to the enroute position as shown in #ref(<fig-handoff>)\.]

  #align(center)[#figure(image("/documents/general/images/handoff-flow.svg", alt: "Release and handoff flow between ZXAA_TWR, ZXAA_APP and ZXEX_CTR", width: 85%), caption: [Release and handoff flow between ZXAA\_TWR, ZXAA\_APP and ZXEX\_CTR]) <fig-handoff>]
] <p602-01-3>

#provision("602.01(3)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The tower asks for a release before an aircraft departs from a runway other than the active one.
] <p602-01-3-a>

#provision("602.01(3)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The approach position grants or refuses the release and may grant a blanket release for a defined set of aircraft.
] <p602-01-3-b>

#provision("602.01(3)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Once the aircraft is identified and climbing, the approach position hands it off to the enroute position. Handoffs are completed before the aircraft reaches the sector boundary.
] <p602-01-3-c>

#provision("602.01(3)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A controller who cannot meet these timings tells the next position as early as possible.
] <p602-01-3-d>

#provision("602.01(4)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(4)", title: [Phraseology])[
  Consistent phraseology reduces misunderstandings.
] <p602-01-4>

#provision("602.01(4)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Controllers use the approved phraseology of the Exampleland authorities.
] <p602-01-4-a>

#provision("602.01(4)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Informal phrases and phraseology from other countries are avoided, even when they seem harmless.
] <p602-01-4-b>

#provision("602.01(4)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A phraseology guide is kept in the controller resources area. If it disagrees with an official source, the official source wins.
] <p602-01-4-c>

#provision("602.01(5)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(5)", title: [Datalink])[
  Datalink messages are an optional way to exchange clearances and requests.
] <p602-01-5>

#provision("602.01(5)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Controllers may offer datalink services but are not required to.
] <p602-01-5-a>

#provision("602.01(5)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The ExampleSitu tool supports departure clearances and enroute messages. Controllers who offer datalink announce it in their controller information.
] <p602-01-5-b>

#provision("602.01(5)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Datalink is not used for busy terminal interactions.
] <p602-01-5-c>

#provision("602.01(6)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(6)", title: [Events])[
  Events bring traffic to the FIR and are planned well in advance.
] <p602-01-6>

#provision("602.01(6)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The Operations Lead approves every event before it is announced.
] <p602-01-6-a>

#provision("602.01(6)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  An event plan names the airports, the positions needed and the expected traffic levels.
] <p602-01-6-b>

#provision("602.01(6)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Controllers who sign up for an event are expected to attend or to give notice as early as possible.
] <p602-01-6-c>

#provision("602.01(6)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  During an event the Operations Lead or a delegate acts as event coordinator and is the point of contact for neighbouring units.
] <p602-01-6-d>

#provision("602.01(7)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(7)", title: [Neighbouring units])[
  The FIR coordinates with neighbouring regions according to written agreements.
] <p602-01-7>

#provision("602.01(7)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Controllers follow the current agreements as published in the resources area.
] <p602-01-7-a>

#provision("602.01(7)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A controller who is unsure of an agreement asks the Operations Lead before acting on an assumption.
] <p602-01-7-b>

#provision("602.01(7)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  New agreements are announced to members before they take effect.
] <p602-01-7-c>

#provision("602.01(8)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(8)", title: [Unusual situations])[
  Controllers sometimes meet situations the handbook does not describe.
] <p602-01-8>

#provision("602.01(8)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  In an unusual situation, safety and clear communication come first.
] <p602-01-8-a>

#provision("602.01(8)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A controller who is unsure asks the next position or a more experienced colleague for advice.
] <p602-01-8-b>

#provision("602.01(8)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Unusual situations are reported to the Operations Lead afterwards so the handbook can be improved.
] <p602-01-8-c>

#provision("602.01(9)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(9)", title: [Tower practice])[
  Tower positions work close to the runway and have the shortest reaction times.
] <p602-01-9>

#provision("602.01(9)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Tower controllers scan the whole movement area before issuing a line-up or take-off clearance.
] <p602-01-9-a>

#provision("602.01(9)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Tower controllers tell the approach position about every departure that does not use the active runway.
] <p602-01-9-b>

#provision("602.01(9)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A tower controller who is unsure of a runway state asks the pilot rather than assuming.
] <p602-01-9-c>

#provision("602.01(9)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A tower controller uses the departure information of the airport in the controller information line.
] <p602-01-9-d>

#provision("602.01(9)(e)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(e)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Tower controllers hand off departing aircraft before they leave the airport boundary.
] <p602-01-9-e>

#provision("602.01(10)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(10)", title: [Terminal practice])[
  Terminal positions sequence arrivals and departures.
] <p602-01-10>

#provision("602.01(10)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Terminal controllers publish the expected approach in the information broadcast.
] <p602-01-10-a>

#provision("602.01(10)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Terminal controllers give arrivals the speed and altitude restrictions in the airport procedures.
] <p602-01-10-b>

#provision("602.01(10)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Terminal controllers keep departures clear of arrivals until separation is established.
] <p602-01-10-c>

#provision("602.01(10)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Terminal controllers tell the tower about expected delays.
] <p602-01-10-d>

#provision("602.01(11)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(11)", title: [Enroute practice])[
  The enroute position covers the whole FIR above the terminal areas.
] <p602-01-11>

#provision("602.01(11)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The enroute controller accepts handoffs from the terminal positions before the aircraft reaches the boundary.
] <p602-01-11-a>

#provision("602.01(11)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The enroute controller uses datalink for routine requests where the pilot supports it.
] <p602-01-11-b>

#provision("602.01(11)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The enroute controller coordinates with neighbouring units before an aircraft leaves the FIR.
] <p602-01-11-c>

#provision("602.01(11)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The enroute controller tells the Operations Lead about any extended period of heavy traffic.
] <p602-01-11-d>

#provision("602.05", 3, level-label: "Section", title: [Software Use])[
  Software helps controllers but it must never get in the way of providing service.
] <p602-05>

#provision("602.05(1)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(1)", title: [Approved tools])[
  Only approved software is used for control sessions.
] <p602-05-1>

#provision("602.05(1)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The current approved list is kept in the resources area and replaces any earlier list.
] <p602-05-1-a>

#provision("602.05(1)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Controllers use the current sector files published by the Tools Lead.
] <p602-05-1-b>

#provision("602.05(1)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Students use only the tools supported by the FIR. More experienced controllers may add other tools provided their service does not suffer.
] <p602-05-1-c>

#provision("602.05(2)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(2)", title: [Information broadcasts])[
  Automated information broadcasts are published only by controllers who may control the airport concerned.
] <p602-05-2>

#provision("602.05(2)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Broadcasts contain only information that can be acted on in the simulation. Items such as closed taxiways or construction activity are left out.
] <p602-05-2-a>

#provision("602.05(2)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The standard weather profiles supplied by the FIR are not modified, except by controllers at the enroute level who may add airport conditions.
] <p602-05-2-b>

#provision("602.05(3)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(3)", title: [Voice and recording], keep: false)[
  Controllers connect to the voice server in an FIR channel before they log on to a position.
] <p602-05-3>

#provision("602.05(3)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Channel nicknames reflect the member's real first name.
] <p602-05-3-a>

#provision("602.05(3)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Controllers do not stay deafened for long periods while connected.
] <p602-05-3-b>

#provision("602.05(3)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Training channels are used for training only.
] <p602-05-3-c>

#provision("602.05(3)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Controllers may stream or record their own sessions when the parent organization's rules allow it. Students on a solo permission or in a training session do not.
] <p602-05-3-d>

#provision("602.05(4)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(4)", title: [Reporting problems])[
  Software sometimes fails.
] <p602-05-4>

#provision("602.05(4)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A controller who finds a fault tells the Tools Lead and gives the steps needed to reproduce it.
] <p602-05-4-a>

#provision("602.05(4)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Controllers do not publish workarounds for faults without the Tools Lead's agreement.
] <p602-05-4-b>

#provision("602.05(4)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Known faults and their workarounds are listed in the resources area.
] <p602-05-4-c>

#provision("602.05(5)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(5)", title: [Additional tools], page-break: true)[
  Controllers may use additional tools to help their service.
] <p602-05-5>

#provision("602.05(5)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Additional tools must not change the information shown to other controllers.
] <p602-05-5-a>

#provision("602.05(5)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A controller who uses an additional tool is able to give the same service without it.
] <p602-05-5-b>

#provision("602.05(5)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The Tools Lead may ask a controller to stop using a tool that causes problems.
] <p602-05-5-c>

#provision("602.05(5)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  New tools are proposed to the Tools Lead before members are encouraged to use them.
] <p602-05-5-d>

#provision("602.08", 3, level-label: "Section", repealed: true)[
  Withdrawn on 2025-03-01; replaced by #link(<p602-05>)[\[602.05\]]\.
] <p602-08>

#provision("602.60", 3, level-label: "Section", title: [Handoff coordination])[
  This section sets out how positions coordinate a handoff in detail.
] <p602-60>

#provision("602.60(1)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(1)", title: [Sequence of a handoff])[

] <p602-60-1>

#provision("602.60(1)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The sending position identifies the aircraft to the receiving position.
] <p602-60-1-a>

#provision("602.60(1)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The receiving position acknowledges the identification and states any restriction.
] <p602-60-1-b>

#provision("602.60(1)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The sending position transfers control only when the aircraft is ready, that is:
] <p602-60-1-c>

#provision("602.60(1)(c)(i)", 6, level-label: "Subparagraph", label: "(i)", indent: 2)[
  the aircraft is established on the agreed route, and
] <p602-60-1-c-i>

#provision("602.60(1)(c)(i)(A)", 7, level-label: "Clause", label: "(A)", indent: 3)[
  the aircraft is identified by the receiving position; and
] <p602-60-1-c-i-A>

#provision("602.60(1)(c)(i)(B)", 7, level-label: "Clause", label: "(B)", indent: 3)[
  the aircraft is clear of conflicting traffic, which means:
] <p602-60-1-c-i-B>

#provision("602.60(1)(c)(i)(B)(I)", 8, level-label: "Subclause", label: "(I)", indent: 4)[
  the required separation exists at the time of transfer; and
] <p602-60-1-c-i-B-I>

#provision("602.60(1)(c)(i)(B)(II)", 8, level-label: "Subclause", label: "(II)", indent: 4)[
  the separation is expected to remain for at least two minutes.
] <p602-60-1-c-i-B-II>

#provision("602.60(1)(c)(ii)", 6, level-label: "Subparagraph", label: "(ii)", indent: 2)[
  the pilot has been told which frequency to contact.
] <p602-60-1-c-ii>

#provision("602.60(2)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(2)", title: [Failed handoffs])[
  A handoff that does not complete is handled as follows.
] <p602-60-2>

#provision("602.60(2)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The sending position keeps the aircraft and informs the receiving position.
] <p602-60-2-a>

#provision("602.60(2)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The aircraft is not turned toward the boundary until the handoff has completed.
] <p602-60-2-b>

#provision("7", 1, level-label: "Part", title: [Administration and Reference], page-break: true)[

] <p7>

#provision("700.01", 3, level-label: "Section", title: [Administration])[
  Administration keeps the FIR running between sessions.
] <p700-01>

#provision("700.01(1)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(1)", title: [Records])[
  The FIR keeps a small number of records and keeps them well.
] <p700-01-1>

#provision("700.01(1)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The roster, training records and assessment results are held in the FIR's central repository.
] <p700-01-1-a>

#provision("700.01(1)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Records are accessible to staff who need them and to nobody else.
] <p700-01-1-b>

#provision("700.01(1)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Assessment records are kept for as long as the member remains in the FIR.
] <p700-01-1-c>

#provision("700.01(2)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(2)", title: [Review cycle])[
  Policy is reviewed on a fixed schedule.
] <p700-01-2>

#provision("700.01(2)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The handbook is reviewed once a year.
] <p700-01-2-a>

#provision("700.01(2)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Practice guides and notices issued under #link(<p600-01-4>)[\[600.01(4)\]] are reviewed every quarter.
] <p700-01-2-b>

#provision("700.01(3)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(3)", title: [Contacts])[
  Questions about this handbook go to the FIR Lead at lead\@example.test.
] <p700-01-3>

#provision("700.01(3)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Questions about training go to the Training Lead at training\@example.test.
] <p700-01-3-a>

#provision("700.01(4)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(4)", repealed: true)[
  Withdrawn on 2025-03-01; replaced by #link(<p700-01-3>)[\[700.01(3)\]]\.
] <p700-01-4>

#provision("700.01(5)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(5)", title: [Complaints])[
  Members may raise a complaint about service or conduct.
] <p700-01-5>

#provision("700.01(5)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Complaints are sent in writing to the FIR Lead.
] <p700-01-5-a>

#provision("700.01(5)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The FIR Lead acknowledges a complaint within seven days and tells the complainant what will happen next.
] <p700-01-5-b>

#provision("700.01(5)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A complaint about the FIR Lead is sent to the parent organization.
] <p700-01-5-c>

#provision("700.01(5)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Complaints are handled in confidence.
] <p700-01-5-d>

#provision("700.01(6)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(6)", title: [Leaving the FIR])[
  Members may leave at any time.
] <p700-01-6>

#provision("700.01(6)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A member who wishes to leave tells the Operations Lead.
] <p700-01-6-a>

#provision("700.01(6)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A member who has left and wishes to return applies again and may be asked to complete a short refresher.
] <p700-01-6-b>

#provision("700.02", 3, level-label: "Section", title: [Organization])[
  The FIR is run by a small team of volunteers.
] <p700-02>

#provision("700.02(1)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(1)", title: [Roles])[
  #block(sticky: true)[The structure of the team is shown in #ref(<fig-org>)\.]

  #align(center)[#figure(image("/documents/general/images/org-chart.svg", alt: "Organization of the Exampleland FIR: the FIR Lead above the Training, Operations and Tools Leads, with mentors and an event team below", width: 80%), caption: [Organization of the Exampleland FIR: the FIR Lead above the Training, Operations and Tools Leads, with mentors and an event team below]) <fig-org>]
] <p700-02-1>

#provision("700.02(1)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The FIR Lead is accountable for the FIR to the parent organization.
] <p700-02-1-a>

#provision("700.02(1)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The Training Lead runs the training program and the mentors.
] <p700-02-1-b>

#provision("700.02(1)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The Operations Lead looks after the roster, currency and events.
] <p700-02-1-c>

#provision("700.02(1)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The Tools Lead maintains sector files and supported software.
] <p700-02-1-d>

#provision("700.02(2)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(2)", title: [Selection of staff])[
  Staff are chosen by the FIR Lead.
] <p700-02-2>

#provision("700.02(2)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A candidate is a home controller in good standing.
] <p700-02-2-a>

#provision("700.02(2)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A candidate shows commitment, patience and good communication, and accepts constructive criticism.
] <p700-02-2-b>

#provision("700.02(2)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A candidate for an instructional role has controlled at least fifty hours in the FIR at the relevant level.
] <p700-02-2-c>

#provision("700.02(3)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(3)", title: [Terms of appointment])[
  Staff appointments have a fixed term.
] <p700-02-3>

#provision("700.02(3)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Appointments last one year and may be renewed.
] <p700-02-3-a>

#provision("700.02(3)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A staff member who resigns tells the FIR Lead at least thirty days beforehand.
] <p700-02-3-b>

#provision("700.02(3)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A staff member hands over records and access to a successor.
] <p700-02-3-c>

#provision("700.02(3)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A staff member who no longer meets the requirements of #link(<p700-02-2>)[\[700.02(2)\]] is replaced.
] <p700-02-3-d>

#provision("700.02(4)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(4)", title: [Meetings])[
  Staff meet regularly.
] <p700-02-4>

#provision("700.02(4)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Staff meetings are held once a month and are open to any member who wishes to listen.
] <p700-02-4-a>

#provision("700.02(4)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Minutes are published within a week of each meeting.
] <p700-02-4-b>

#provision("700.02(4)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  Decisions that change policy are recorded in the handbook through the normal amendment process.
] <p700-02-4-c>

